1
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:04,800
Let's break up.

2
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:06,840
<i>I can't date someone</i>
<i>who's in love with my best friend.</i>

3
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:08,720
We know about you and Lee.

4
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,040
I could've let it go that you lied to me.

5
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:12,440
But I can't.

6
00:00:12,520 --> 00:00:13,480
I'm quitting this club.

7
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:15,360
<i>I never wanted to be</i>
<i>in this damn club anyway.</i>

8
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:16,440
"DON'T" DATE SOMEONE CLOSE TO YOU!

9
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:17,960
Welcome, everyone,

10
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:21,200
to Next Gen E-sports Thailand.

11
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:22,520
Hey!

12
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:24,640
Putter, you can do this! I believe in you!

13
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:27,920
And the winner of this qualifier is Team…

14
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,280
Fire Storm!

15
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:32,240
Let's just go back to being friends.

16
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:35,960
I think it'd be better for us
and everyone else, don't you?

17
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:38,640
<i>Love and friendship.</i>

18
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:41,080
<i>are equally hard to walk away from.</i>

19
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:44,600
<i>Especially when you two</i>
<i>already broke up, but he's still around.</i>

20
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:46,200
<i>Then it's even harder.</i>

21
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:48,800
<i>So, you encouraged them</i>
<i>to talk things out?</i>

22
00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:49,840
<i>Yeah.</i>

23
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:52,200
<i>Otherwise, it would just stay unclear.</i>

24
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:53,800
<i>That would be hard on everyone.</i>

25
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:55,800
<i>If you change your mind, let me know.</i>

26
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:57,720
<i>I think he wants you there.</i>

27
00:00:57,800 --> 00:00:58,920
<i>Yeah.</i>

28
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,920
<i>I told him.</i>

29
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:04,720
<i>Friendship is precious,</i>
<i>and it lasts the longest.</i>

30
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:07,560
<i>But… it's hard to say something like that.</i>

31
00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:12,000
<i>It might sound funny,</i>
<i>but that day, I practiced.</i>

32
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:13,880
<i>I rehearsed my speech before seeing him.</i>

33
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:18,720
<i>All this… is just to tell you…</i>

34
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:21,760
<i>I like you.</i>

35
00:01:22,360 --> 00:01:24,480
<i>Break the rule… and be my boyfriend.</i>

36
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:26,280
<i>Shit.</i>

37
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:28,680
<i>What the hell am I saying?</i>

38
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:42,000
<i>Putter.</i>

39
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:46,000
<i>I believe you, that you don't like Indy.</i>

40
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:49,600
<i>But right now,</i>

41
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:53,960
<i>I'm afraid… I'll end up</i>
<i>feeling this way again.</i>

42
00:01:56,760 --> 00:02:00,960
We might get back together
just to break up again.

43
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:03,360
And I don't want to lose you.

44
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,880
It's just… I think…

45
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:09,000
<i>Let's go back to being friends.</i>

46
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:18,680
It'd be better for us… and everyone else.

47
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:20,440
Don't you think?

48
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:24,720
<i>I practiced this.</i>

49
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:28,080
<i>But when I saw you,</i>
<i>I still couldn't say it all.</i>

50
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:36,920
Yeah. I agree.

51
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:40,600
We'll get to mess with each other again.

52
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:44,560
Staying like this
has been so damn awkward.

53
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:47,000
I'm tired of acting.

54
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:54,440
So… friends again, okay?

55
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:04,520
Yeah, of course.
Want me to smack you to prove it?

56
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:06,040
Hey, no, thanks.

57
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:08,360
Do something friends would do.
Don't be ridiculous.

58
00:03:12,040 --> 00:03:13,040
Fine.

59
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:15,120
Then I'll roast you myself.

60
00:03:16,760 --> 00:03:19,200
Roast me at the restaurant. I'm starving.

61
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:34,120
Do you think… they'll get back together?

62
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:37,600
- I think they'll get back together.
- I don't think so.

63
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:41,560
Yeah. Which way's the restaurant?

64
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:44,400
That way.

65
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:45,400
Let's go.

66
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:50,680
You don't have to carry it. I'll carry it.

67
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:54,560
Your loss. Less work for me.

68
00:03:58,960 --> 00:04:00,200
<i>They're here.</i>
<i>Let's pretend we don't see them.</i>

69
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:01,560
<i>They're here.</i>

70
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:03,520
<i>- They're here.</i>
<i>- They're here.</i>

71
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:04,440
Come on.

72
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:06,920
- Go, go, go.
- Hurry, hurry.

73
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:07,960
You go.

74
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:09,440
- Go already.
- Go on.

75
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:10,960
You go too.

76
00:05:40,200 --> 00:05:42,360
My stomach's about to burst.

77
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:46,520
Whoa.

78
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:49,800
With the lights on,
the room feels so much brighter.

79
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:51,920
Yeah, totally.

80
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,320
Last week, I thought
you were saving electricity.

81
00:05:56,840 --> 00:05:58,400
I was just going for a dark vibe.

82
00:05:58,960 --> 00:06:02,560
Update your patch.
Nobody's that dark anymore.

83
00:06:04,400 --> 00:06:06,920
- Don't kill the mood.
- What?

84
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:11,320
Nothing. Nothing.

85
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:16,000
Got a little reward for you.
In the fridge.

86
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:18,520
To celebrate you, Putter… and Fire Storm.

87
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:19,480
Go check it out.

88
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:21,240
- Yeah, I'm going.
- Go on, hurry.

89
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:30,280
You bought five boxes? This many?

90
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:32,600
I'm gonna get so fat. Let's share them.

91
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:35,840
I bought that many…
just to hear you say that.

92
00:06:37,520 --> 00:06:38,800
Always scheming,
then calling it friendship.

93
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:41,800
But… Thanks anyway.

94
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:52,160
I got it from here.

95
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:09,520
You gonna take a shower?

96
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:10,920
If not, mind if I go first?

97
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,320
Yeah.

98
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:15,400
I'm glad… we're talking again.

99
00:07:16,400 --> 00:07:18,440
Yeah. Me too.

100
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:22,280
And… don't forget
to clear things up with Indy.

101
00:07:22,360 --> 00:07:23,480
- Yeah.
- You're the only one left.

102
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:24,680
Okay.

103
00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:27,880
See you tomorrow, Buddy.

104
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:31,640
See you. Buddy.

105
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:35,039
Shit. Sorry, traffic was awful.

106
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:09,360
Nobody else is here yet?

107
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:18,520
Guess they're running late.

108
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:24,120
Didn't think you'd come.

109
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:29,040
I… came to make things right.

110
00:09:34,440 --> 00:09:37,480
I'll go grab some drinks,
if nobody's here yet.

111
00:09:40,400 --> 00:09:41,280
Wait.

112
00:09:44,240 --> 00:09:45,360
I'll come with you.

113
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:47,600
What do you want? I'll get it.

114
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:52,480
It's just…

115
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:56,000
I've got something to talk to you about.

116
00:09:58,360 --> 00:10:01,360
Come on. Been waiting for you to start.

117
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:04,080
If you say some stupid shit again,
I'm punching you.

118
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:10,440
Want a free punch first?

119
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:11,960
I'm not a violent person.

120
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:14,360
You're full of shit.

121
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:22,360
I… I'm sorry.

122
00:10:23,120 --> 00:10:26,000
For… being such an idiot.

123
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:28,240
None of it was your fault.

124
00:10:30,360 --> 00:10:33,080
Yeah. You were way out of line.

125
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:35,320
Yeah. I'll take the blame for everything.

126
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:38,680
I'll…

127
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:41,040
buy you ten meals.

128
00:10:42,560 --> 00:10:44,280
That's all you've got to say?

129
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:48,520
Here.

130
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:52,480
We've already had our deep talk.
Have a seat.

131
00:11:00,760 --> 00:11:03,760
Didn't think I'd say this today,
but I'll say it.

132
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:10,920
You… are the closest friend I've ever had.

133
00:11:13,520 --> 00:11:17,840
I… don't want anything…
to change what we have.

134
00:11:20,760 --> 00:11:22,240
The reason I got mad…

135
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:26,000
was because I felt…

136
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:28,800
like your replacement.

137
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:33,520
I couldn't bring myself to be mad
at Putter, so I took it out on you.

138
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:36,560
Which… I don't even know why.

139
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:43,560
But no matter what,
I shouldn't have done that.

140
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:46,200
I shouldn't have lied to you.

141
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:48,360
Because you…

142
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:55,120
care about me more than anyone.

143
00:11:57,640 --> 00:11:58,920
And I…

144
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:02,040
care about you the most too.

145
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:33,440
Honestly, I never thought…
we'd ever fight over love.

146
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:35,560
Pretty cool.

147
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:48,640
Oh, shit.

148
00:12:48,720 --> 00:12:50,360
I'm keeping this to blackmail you.

149
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:53,520
If you ever act like an asshole again,
I'm posting every single one, dumbass.

150
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:55,600
- So you were acting?
- Nope.

151
00:12:55,680 --> 00:12:57,840
I really was mad, just not that mad.

152
00:13:02,520 --> 00:13:04,120
Just don't do it again.

153
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,560
That shitty attitude.

154
00:13:07,640 --> 00:13:08,840
Yes, Dad.

155
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:12,000
This is something new, though.

156
00:13:12,760 --> 00:13:16,320
All the time we've been friends,
we've never thrown a punch.

157
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:19,640
Never had a real fight.

158
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:22,400
I actually want to complete
the best-friend checklist.

159
00:13:25,520 --> 00:13:27,600
I'll give you one. Want it?

160
00:13:27,680 --> 00:13:29,000
- Hell yeah, asshole.
- Hey, wait.

161
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:30,800
- What's with you?
- Let me punch you first.

162
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:46,160
- Surprise!
- Surprise!

163
00:13:48,480 --> 00:13:49,880
I knew it.

164
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:52,160
If all of you were late,
it would be the end of the world.

165
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:53,360
Yeah, whatever.

166
00:13:53,440 --> 00:13:55,440
Come on, let's take a picture.

167
00:13:55,520 --> 00:13:57,600
- I'm sending it to our group.
- Go, go.

168
00:13:57,680 --> 00:13:58,760
Go, go!

169
00:13:58,840 --> 00:14:00,560
- Put your arms around each other.
- Closer.

170
00:14:00,640 --> 00:14:01,560
That's it!

171
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:04,040
Click.

172
00:14:49,120 --> 00:14:50,240
Putter.

173
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:52,920
I'm sorry.

174
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,960
That's enough. You're embarrassing me.

175
00:14:55,040 --> 00:14:56,360
I said wait for the right moment.

176
00:14:56,440 --> 00:14:58,440
Well, this is it.
Otherwise, I'll lose my nerve.

177
00:14:58,520 --> 00:15:01,360
- I'm sorry. I'm really sorry, Putter.
- That's enough!

178
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,960
I saw that you like sweets.
So I bought you some desserts.

179
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:09,480
I'm really sorry, Putter.

180
00:15:09,560 --> 00:15:12,000
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry. I really am.

181
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:13,640
I really didn't know.

182
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:16,480
You weren't the one
who leaked the clip, right?

183
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:18,720
No. I wasn't the one who leaked it.

184
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:20,280
Tell him that.

185
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:23,560
Well, if you apologize like that…
anyone would think you leaked it.

186
00:15:24,760 --> 00:15:26,320
I'm really sorry. I really am.

187
00:15:26,920 --> 00:15:29,240
I just feel so guilty.

188
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:31,120
Normally, I'm all for shipping moments,

189
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:33,880
and when they're real, it's even better.

190
00:15:33,960 --> 00:15:35,520
- Honestly…
- That's enough, Min.

191
00:15:35,600 --> 00:15:36,920
You're making it worse.

192
00:15:38,760 --> 00:15:40,160
I'm sorry.

193
00:15:40,680 --> 00:15:44,160
But when it happened to you…
my best friend,

194
00:15:44,240 --> 00:15:46,080
I felt even worse

195
00:15:46,160 --> 00:15:48,360
for enjoying something
you wanted to keep private.

196
00:15:49,840 --> 00:15:50,960
I'm sorry.

197
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:54,240
Thank you so much, Min,
for caring about me this much.

198
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:57,400
I was a little upset,
when people dug this up.

199
00:15:59,360 --> 00:16:01,080
But… I'm over it.

200
00:16:05,480 --> 00:16:06,600
- Really?
- Really.

201
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:12,240
So… stop feeling guilty. I forgive you.

202
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:17,480
Nobody's fighting anymore.

203
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:18,680
LeeIth and I…

204
00:16:21,840 --> 00:16:22,680
are good again.

205
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:27,480
Come on. You just apologized to him.

206
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:33,960
I mean… LeeIth and I… are friends again.

207
00:16:51,320 --> 00:16:52,640
Cheers.

208
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:57,600
- Hey!
- Hey.

209
00:16:57,680 --> 00:16:58,720
- Hey!
- Hello.

210
00:16:58,800 --> 00:17:01,000
- Sit here.
- You bought so many desserts.

211
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:01,920
Here you go.

212
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:03,640
- Where's mine?
- Here.

213
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:05,280
Come sit down. Sit.

214
00:17:05,359 --> 00:17:06,760
Hurry, sit.

215
00:17:06,839 --> 00:17:08,440
- Yeah, I'm coming.
- Wait for me.

216
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:11,119
I'll put the cups here.

217
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:12,440
- Go ahead, sit.
- Okay.

218
00:17:13,319 --> 00:17:15,520
- Have a seat.
- Everyone.

219
00:17:15,599 --> 00:17:18,240
Finally, we saved our friendship.

220
00:17:20,079 --> 00:17:22,040
We did it!

221
00:17:22,119 --> 00:17:23,800
Oh, come on.

222
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:25,359
- Keep it up.
- You're way too excited.

223
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:26,760
Including me?

224
00:17:26,839 --> 00:17:28,840
Of course. Today wouldn't be
complete without you.

225
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:31,040
Hey, everyone, look!

226
00:17:31,120 --> 00:17:33,160
Leo's sitting with everyone today.

227
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:36,160
Scoot over. Hurry.

228
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:38,800
We're friends now.

229
00:17:38,880 --> 00:17:40,080
Well…

230
00:17:40,720 --> 00:17:43,280
- Okay, okay.
- I'm still excited.

231
00:17:43,360 --> 00:17:45,960
Just to be safe, I'll sit over there.

232
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:49,160
- Ditching me?
- You seem relaxed today.

233
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:52,640
Nothing but good news today.
What? What else?

234
00:17:52,720 --> 00:17:54,000
Hit me with all of it!

235
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:55,280
There is!

236
00:17:55,360 --> 00:17:59,000
We, Lazy Meow Meow…
are playing our first competition at Siam!

237
00:18:01,840 --> 00:18:03,920
Lazy Meow Meow!

238
00:18:04,520 --> 00:18:06,840
- Come on, scream!
- Keep going! Don't interrupt. What else?

239
00:18:06,920 --> 00:18:09,120
- Me! Me!
- Go ahead!

240
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:11,600
This better be huge, asshole.

241
00:18:11,680 --> 00:18:15,040
It is. Faye and I are officially together!

242
00:18:16,440 --> 00:18:18,040
I knew it!

243
00:18:18,120 --> 00:18:20,360
- In! Faye! In! Faye!
- Indy actually did it!

244
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:21,840
Didn't you say Faye
always left you on read?

245
00:18:21,920 --> 00:18:23,280
I could handle that.

246
00:18:23,360 --> 00:18:25,040
When did you two start dating?

247
00:18:25,120 --> 00:18:26,960
Yeah, and how did it even happen?

248
00:18:28,800 --> 00:18:30,800
Because of the love note.

249
00:18:33,240 --> 00:18:35,840
<i>I'm so sick,</i>
<i>and I'm sick of this. Allergies.</i>

250
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:39,040
<i>Get well soon.</i>

251
00:18:42,120 --> 00:18:43,760
<i>Thank you, Indy.</i>

252
00:18:43,840 --> 00:18:45,720
<i>That's where our story began.</i>

253
00:18:45,800 --> 00:18:46,640
1/2 FOOD

254
00:18:51,560 --> 00:18:53,400
<i>Make sure to eat… and take your medicine.</i>

255
00:18:55,480 --> 00:18:58,560
<i>I brought meals…</i>
<i>and medicine to Faye all week long.</i>

256
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:06,480
Indy.

257
00:19:09,320 --> 00:19:10,480
Faye.

258
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:22,200
Thank you, Indy.

259
00:19:22,280 --> 00:19:23,920
The medicine worked wonders.

260
00:19:25,320 --> 00:19:27,040
You're welcome.

261
00:19:27,120 --> 00:19:30,080
Then I'll… get going.

262
00:19:39,680 --> 00:19:40,680
Wait.

263
00:19:41,600 --> 00:19:44,800
- Can I ask you something?
- Sure.

264
00:19:46,840 --> 00:19:51,200
From now on…
would you bring me meals every day?

265
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:02,880
You mean…

266
00:20:14,320 --> 00:20:17,680
Woo-hoo!

267
00:20:18,360 --> 00:20:20,160
My friend's got a girlfriend!

268
00:20:20,240 --> 00:20:21,800
Put your head on her shoulder!

269
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:23,680
How are you this smooth?

270
00:20:25,040 --> 00:20:26,280
Something like that.

271
00:20:26,360 --> 00:20:29,800
Proud of me, Doc? Making my own decisions?

272
00:20:31,560 --> 00:20:33,000
How's it going with Faye?

273
00:20:33,080 --> 00:20:35,240
Let me know when you two get married.

274
00:20:36,960 --> 00:20:40,760
- Indy! Indy!
- Cut it out, asshole.

275
00:20:40,840 --> 00:20:43,040
I'll keep you updated.

276
00:20:46,840 --> 00:20:48,600
I'm already getting ready for the wedding.

277
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:50,840
<i>Did you see what I sent you?</i>

278
00:20:50,920 --> 00:20:52,560
Which outfit should I wear?

279
00:20:52,640 --> 00:20:54,560
<i>You said you didn't need</i>
<i>my help deciding anymore.</i>

280
00:20:55,800 --> 00:20:57,080
Are you sulking?

281
00:20:57,600 --> 00:20:58,720
No.

282
00:20:58,800 --> 00:21:00,600
It's just that some dog asked,

283
00:21:00,680 --> 00:21:03,480
"Are you proud of me
for making my own decisions?"

284
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:08,080
Well, Faye's really serious
about dressing up.

285
00:21:08,600 --> 00:21:10,080
I'm only asking you to pick an outfit.

286
00:21:10,160 --> 00:21:12,160
Not to choose my path in life.

287
00:21:13,320 --> 00:21:15,360
<i>You're still asking me to decide for you.</i>

288
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:18,720
Fine. I'll choose it myself.

289
00:21:18,800 --> 00:21:21,720
<i>Think Faye and I will work out?</i>

290
00:21:22,240 --> 00:21:24,840
Why ask me? What's making you hesitate?

291
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:28,080
Don't know. I just feel… weird.

292
00:21:28,160 --> 00:21:31,960
Like… my heart's not beating normally.

293
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:35,040
<i>Maybe you should see a doctor.</i>

294
00:21:35,800 --> 00:21:38,240
I am. Fortune Teller Jia's right here.

295
00:21:38,320 --> 00:21:39,600
Draw me a card.

296
00:21:48,880 --> 00:21:50,720
One question, then let me sleep.

297
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:04,720
<i>Calm down… and think of that person.</i>
<i>The one you like.</i>

298
00:22:06,120 --> 00:22:08,040
The one you feel at ease with.

299
00:22:28,480 --> 00:22:30,120
<i>Your mind's not settled. I can't read it.</i>

300
00:22:33,880 --> 00:22:35,960
How… did you know?

301
00:22:36,040 --> 00:22:37,280
You're shaking even more now.

302
00:22:39,280 --> 00:22:42,120
Then never mind. Good night.

303
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:02,280
Will this one do?

304
00:23:06,240 --> 00:23:07,640
It's pretty good.

305
00:23:07,720 --> 00:23:10,880
Or if you don't like it,
I can take another one.

306
00:23:10,960 --> 00:23:14,120
It's okay. Let me take some
of you instead.

307
00:23:16,960 --> 00:23:17,920
Here we go.

308
00:23:18,760 --> 00:23:20,640
One… two…

309
00:23:20,720 --> 00:23:22,760
Move a little to the left.

310
00:23:22,840 --> 00:23:24,680
Lean forward a little.

311
00:23:24,760 --> 00:23:25,640
Okay.

312
00:23:28,040 --> 00:23:29,120
That's a shame.

313
00:23:29,200 --> 00:23:31,320
Your outfit doesn't really match
the café today.

314
00:23:35,480 --> 00:23:36,600
Really?

315
00:23:37,600 --> 00:23:39,440
I thought you'd coordinate your outfit.

316
00:23:41,280 --> 00:23:42,200
That's news to me.

317
00:23:42,800 --> 00:23:44,720
Didn't know I had to match my outfit too.

318
00:23:44,800 --> 00:23:47,320
Let's try again next time.
You'll get better photos.

319
00:23:48,760 --> 00:23:49,680
Let's eat.

320
00:24:01,320 --> 00:24:04,280
- You seem a little nervous.
- Do I?

321
00:24:04,360 --> 00:24:06,040
FORTUNE TELLER JIA

322
00:24:11,320 --> 00:24:12,240
Hello?

323
00:24:13,640 --> 00:24:14,600
<i>Where are you?</i>

324
00:24:15,800 --> 00:24:16,920
You okay?

325
00:24:18,320 --> 00:24:19,920
<i>We can talk when you're free.</i>

326
00:24:20,560 --> 00:24:21,800
<i>I'm still okay.</i>

327
00:24:36,480 --> 00:24:38,440
I'm in the middle of the bridge.

328
00:24:38,520 --> 00:24:40,000
<i>Me too.</i>

329
00:24:40,080 --> 00:24:44,240
<i>There's lotus flowers…</i>
<i>banana trees… and a waterfall.</i>

330
00:24:44,320 --> 00:24:45,360
<i>And trees.</i>

331
00:24:46,520 --> 00:24:47,960
- I see you.
<i>- Have you found me yet?</i>

332
00:25:01,080 --> 00:25:02,920
Hop on.

333
00:25:05,920 --> 00:25:08,040
I'll pedal. You just sit there.

334
00:25:10,640 --> 00:25:11,760
Let's go.

335
00:25:15,520 --> 00:25:16,800
Careful. Pedestrians.

336
00:25:43,640 --> 00:25:45,040
So? Having fun?

337
00:25:45,120 --> 00:25:47,200
Yeah… but I'm exhausted.

338
00:25:55,880 --> 00:25:57,040
You okay?

339
00:25:58,720 --> 00:25:59,880
I'm fine.

340
00:26:01,400 --> 00:26:03,520
Remember… what I told you?

341
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:05,680
What the cards say isn't always true.

342
00:26:06,680 --> 00:26:07,520
Yeah.

343
00:26:10,120 --> 00:26:12,840
The cards once showed
my parents would fall in love again.

344
00:26:14,800 --> 00:26:16,080
But they didn't.

345
00:26:46,040 --> 00:26:47,920
You can let your guard down with me.

346
00:26:52,760 --> 00:26:57,360
Breathe in. Breathe out.

347
00:26:57,440 --> 00:27:00,960
Let everything bottled up inside out.

348
00:27:04,760 --> 00:27:06,400
You're making fun of my mom, asshole.

349
00:27:08,520 --> 00:27:09,920
But I tried it, and it really works.

350
00:27:10,520 --> 00:27:12,000
That's because you did it in a room.

351
00:27:12,080 --> 00:27:15,120
Standing there… throwing leaves at me.
Nothing to be embarrassed about.

352
00:27:16,320 --> 00:27:18,320
Come on, I'll do it with you.

353
00:27:23,000 --> 00:27:25,480
Come on. Together.

354
00:27:26,320 --> 00:27:27,720
One…

355
00:27:27,800 --> 00:27:29,160
Two…

356
00:27:29,240 --> 00:27:30,200
Three…

357
00:27:30,280 --> 00:27:32,000
Breathe in.

358
00:27:32,840 --> 00:27:33,960
Breathe out.

359
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:37,480
Breathe in.

360
00:27:38,480 --> 00:27:39,880
Breathe out.

361
00:27:44,240 --> 00:27:46,400
Let those feelings out. Breathe out.

362
00:27:51,520 --> 00:27:54,000
Come on, one last time.

363
00:27:54,080 --> 00:27:55,560
Breathe in.

364
00:27:55,640 --> 00:27:58,000
Let those bottled-up feelings out.

365
00:28:18,560 --> 00:28:20,440
So? Feeling better?

366
00:28:20,520 --> 00:28:22,360
Even more extreme than what my mom does.

367
00:28:23,360 --> 00:28:24,680
But it does feel liberating.

368
00:28:26,320 --> 00:28:27,280
Thanks.

369
00:28:35,120 --> 00:28:37,400
And you being here with me…

370
00:28:37,480 --> 00:28:39,000
Won't Faye mind?

371
00:28:41,120 --> 00:28:42,040
Well…

372
00:28:43,080 --> 00:28:44,040
She won't.

373
00:28:46,120 --> 00:28:48,880
Faye. I'll get going now.

374
00:28:48,960 --> 00:28:50,680
I have something urgent to take care of.

375
00:29:00,760 --> 00:29:03,200
Let's go get some snacks.
Let's get some sugar.

376
00:29:03,280 --> 00:29:04,480
Sure.

377
00:29:13,160 --> 00:29:14,080
Your bag.

378
00:29:25,960 --> 00:29:28,640
- School's over. Want to go to Siam?
- Nah.

379
00:29:28,720 --> 00:29:30,520
Today's our anniversary.

380
00:29:30,600 --> 00:29:32,720
- We're going to celebrate.
- LeeIth.

381
00:29:34,560 --> 00:29:36,240
I came over to say hi, LeeIth.

382
00:29:36,320 --> 00:29:37,920
You can just call me "Lee."

383
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:40,000
Okay.

384
00:29:40,080 --> 00:29:42,640
This is actually my first time
meeting you in person.

385
00:29:42,720 --> 00:29:45,000
Same here. Nice to meet you.

386
00:29:46,000 --> 00:29:48,840
Then I'll text you later.

387
00:29:48,920 --> 00:29:50,560
Okay. Bye-bye.

388
00:29:55,840 --> 00:29:56,760
Your friend?

389
00:29:57,560 --> 00:30:00,960
Yeah. Lately, she's been
trying to hit on me.

390
00:30:02,200 --> 00:30:03,040
She's hitting on him.

391
00:30:03,120 --> 00:30:06,800
You know, I think…
this one doesn't seem closeted.

392
00:30:07,680 --> 00:30:09,640
I've been pretty open lately.

393
00:30:10,240 --> 00:30:12,720
Open-minded. Yeah.

394
00:30:12,800 --> 00:30:15,480
After tutoring, want to head back with me?

395
00:30:16,040 --> 00:30:19,080
I… was planning to watch
a movie at Paragon.

396
00:30:20,760 --> 00:30:21,600
Sure.

397
00:30:34,880 --> 00:30:35,800
Here you go.

398
00:30:44,400 --> 00:30:45,600
Here, this is for you.

399
00:30:51,640 --> 00:30:54,160
<i>Who's cheering for me? Let me hear you!</i>

400
00:30:55,680 --> 00:30:56,840
<i>Thank you…</i>

401
00:31:03,400 --> 00:31:04,280
Want some?

402
00:31:07,720 --> 00:31:08,640
No, thanks.

403
00:31:15,520 --> 00:31:17,240
Fantastic Four is out now.

404
00:31:19,160 --> 00:31:20,880
Yeah. Have you seen it yet?

405
00:31:21,480 --> 00:31:23,960
Not yet. I was planning to watch it today.

406
00:31:24,040 --> 00:31:27,280
I heard the new phase is pretty exciting.

407
00:31:28,000 --> 00:31:29,240
Want to go watch it?

408
00:31:30,520 --> 00:31:32,880
It's okay. I've changed my mind.

409
00:31:32,960 --> 00:31:35,160
I'd rather not watch it.
Come on, let's go upstairs.

410
00:31:53,160 --> 00:31:55,080
- Hey.
- Putter.

411
00:31:56,520 --> 00:31:58,120
- Here, eat.
- Hey, hey, hey!

412
00:31:58,200 --> 00:31:59,760
- Go ahead, eat.
- Have some of my drink.

413
00:31:59,840 --> 00:32:02,040
- Go on, eat.
- Want some snacks?

414
00:32:02,120 --> 00:32:03,440
That's enough.

415
00:32:03,520 --> 00:32:04,800
This is getting a little too sweet.

416
00:32:04,880 --> 00:32:07,480
Come on. We don't want
our friend to feel lonely.

417
00:32:07,560 --> 00:32:10,000
Look, Proud even postponed
where we're going to celebrate

418
00:32:10,080 --> 00:32:11,480
just so she could see you off.

419
00:32:13,280 --> 00:32:15,720
We're Putter's bodyguard squad.

420
00:32:15,800 --> 00:32:17,720
Oh, you're so cringe.

421
00:32:17,800 --> 00:32:19,880
So, are you into bodyguard plots?

422
00:32:19,960 --> 00:32:22,640
Obviously! I love them!

423
00:32:24,840 --> 00:32:27,880
The store where I'm a member
is offering 50% off.

424
00:32:27,960 --> 00:32:28,840
Let's go buy something.

425
00:32:29,440 --> 00:32:30,760
- Hurry up!
- That sounds good!

426
00:32:30,840 --> 00:32:32,520
You keep sulking. I'll be right back.

427
00:32:32,600 --> 00:32:35,000
- Go!
- Hurry up!

428
00:32:35,600 --> 00:32:36,880
One day, it'll get better.

429
00:32:36,960 --> 00:32:39,360
If you want to be sad, then be sad.

430
00:32:39,440 --> 00:32:41,560
You can move on whenever you're ready.

431
00:32:41,640 --> 00:32:43,200
People can't control their feelings.

432
00:32:43,280 --> 00:32:44,720
That's advice from an emotional girl.

433
00:32:46,600 --> 00:32:49,360
Okay. Then you'll be
seeing me sad for a while.

434
00:32:49,440 --> 00:32:51,160
I'm ready.

435
00:32:55,320 --> 00:32:56,840
Hey, you guys go on ahead.

436
00:32:56,920 --> 00:32:58,120
Go, go, go!

437
00:33:14,280 --> 00:33:19,880
NEED ADVICE? ASK LEE

438
00:33:19,960 --> 00:33:22,920
This chat's been dead for ages.
Why did you come in here?

439
00:33:23,560 --> 00:33:25,760
I need your advice about something.

440
00:33:26,640 --> 00:33:28,760
It's about Faye.

441
00:33:30,280 --> 00:33:32,760
Faye's been acting
kind of weird around me.

442
00:33:32,840 --> 00:33:35,120
Everyone keeps messaging me,
asking what I did.

443
00:33:35,200 --> 00:33:36,920
They all say I look better now.

444
00:33:37,000 --> 00:33:41,080
I want to buy more clothes.
Can you take me to Siam again?

445
00:33:41,160 --> 00:33:42,320
FAYE

446
00:33:42,400 --> 00:33:44,400
- <i>And then I… I mean, she…</i>
- She didn't tell you

447
00:33:44,480 --> 00:33:47,320
- <i>thinks Jia and I are really close.</i>
- to tell someone else about it.

448
00:33:49,720 --> 00:33:50,800
<i>She didn't say anything.</i>

449
00:33:50,880 --> 00:33:54,000
<i>She just keeps asking me about Jia.</i>

450
00:33:54,080 --> 00:33:55,520
<i>Here's the thing, though.</i>

451
00:33:56,600 --> 00:33:58,560
I just feel guilty that I…

452
00:33:59,160 --> 00:34:02,480
<i>that I feel more comfortable</i>
<i>being with Jia than Faye.</i>

453
00:34:02,560 --> 00:34:05,120
I feel like talking to him more than Faye.

454
00:34:06,720 --> 00:34:08,239
Do you want my opinion?

455
00:34:08,320 --> 00:34:11,120
Of course I do.
If I didn't, I wouldn't be here.

456
00:34:12,639 --> 00:34:14,719
As your Best Friend of the Year
for seven years…

457
00:34:16,159 --> 00:34:17,199
Making fun of me?

458
00:34:17,760 --> 00:34:22,159
<i>I think… you're starting to fall for Jia.</i>
<i>You're totally hooked on him.</i>

459
00:34:24,280 --> 00:34:28,560
Honestly, I feel that way too,
but… I just needed someone to confirm it.

460
00:34:32,560 --> 00:34:33,520
But…

461
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:36,320
I think

462
00:34:38,080 --> 00:34:40,320
dating someone close to you
never works out.

463
00:34:42,120 --> 00:34:44,040
<i>There'll probably be problems someday.</i>

464
00:34:45,440 --> 00:34:47,320
<i>But the biggest shame is…</i>

465
00:34:48,840 --> 00:34:50,400
losing the friendship.

466
00:34:55,120 --> 00:34:56,719
That's why I came to you.

467
00:34:58,120 --> 00:35:00,920
So… who did you go see a movie with?

468
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:03,000
I was trying to keep
an open mind and move on.

469
00:35:04,520 --> 00:35:06,160
But I'm still going in circles.

470
00:35:09,080 --> 00:35:10,280
Lee, I…

471
00:35:12,040 --> 00:35:13,880
- Huh?
- Hey, Lee.

472
00:35:13,960 --> 00:35:16,280
I made shrimp rice porridge. Want some?

473
00:35:16,360 --> 00:35:18,040
Sure. Thank you.

474
00:35:20,080 --> 00:35:22,120
- Want some?
- Yeah. Bring it over.

475
00:35:41,000 --> 00:35:42,680
<i>Then how about we go see Fantastic Four?</i>

476
00:35:47,480 --> 00:35:50,840
<i>Someone asked me</i>
<i>to see a movie that day, but I…</i>

477
00:35:51,440 --> 00:35:53,560
<i>Sorry, I have something urgent today.</i>

478
00:35:53,640 --> 00:35:55,120
<i>Let's do it another time.</i>

479
00:35:58,680 --> 00:36:01,000
<i>That's too bad, but it's okay.</i>

480
00:36:01,600 --> 00:36:03,320
<i>I just got to Paragon.</i>

481
00:36:08,920 --> 00:36:10,760
<i>If you really want to move on,</i>

482
00:36:10,840 --> 00:36:14,360
<i>Jia once told me to try something new.</i>

483
00:36:14,440 --> 00:36:17,000
Yeah. I did.

484
00:36:17,840 --> 00:36:20,680
<i>You have to be serious about it.</i>
<i>Like I was.</i>

485
00:36:20,760 --> 00:36:25,480
<i>Back then, I… bought new clothes,</i>
<i>found new things to do,</i>

486
00:36:25,560 --> 00:36:27,160
<i>and deleted all of Faye's contacts.</i>

487
00:36:27,960 --> 00:36:29,720
Then how did you get back together?

488
00:36:30,400 --> 00:36:32,520
I thought I'd already moved on.

489
00:36:32,600 --> 00:36:34,840
<i>So I followed her on Instagram again.</i>

490
00:36:34,920 --> 00:36:37,560
- So, did you actually move on?
<i>- Good question.</i>

491
00:36:37,640 --> 00:36:39,080
Does that even count as moving on?

492
00:36:39,160 --> 00:36:40,360
What's wrong with us?

493
00:37:18,920 --> 00:37:22,160
Damn. Chicken rice, thigh meat, no skin.

494
00:37:23,240 --> 00:37:26,040
Yeah. I finished making it,
then remembered you like it.

495
00:37:51,640 --> 00:37:52,600
How is it?

496
00:37:54,280 --> 00:37:55,320
It's pretty good.

497
00:37:56,760 --> 00:37:57,760
And it was free.

498
00:37:58,560 --> 00:37:59,920
I won't starve this month.

499
00:38:01,120 --> 00:38:02,720
Yeah, eat up.

500
00:38:27,880 --> 00:38:29,160
Don't rush. You'll choke.

501
00:38:29,240 --> 00:38:30,920
I'm running late. I have band practice.

502
00:38:32,200 --> 00:38:34,880
No, no, no. I'll clean up.

503
00:38:36,160 --> 00:38:37,240
You're the best, Buddy.

504
00:39:05,160 --> 00:39:08,560
<i>Trying to make conversation</i>
<i>with you here is kind of exhausting.</i>

505
00:39:22,280 --> 00:39:26,600
THANKS. I'M READY FOR TOMORROW.

506
00:39:26,680 --> 00:39:32,760
LAZY MEOW MEOW - WE'RE READY
PLEASE COME SEE US, EVERYONE.

507
00:39:39,400 --> 00:39:41,960
"Lazy Meow Meow." What the heck is that?

508
00:39:43,720 --> 00:39:47,240
- It's our band's name.
- Seriously?

509
00:39:47,880 --> 00:39:49,880
I've wondered about that too.

510
00:39:49,960 --> 00:39:51,720
The band's name is one thing,

511
00:39:51,800 --> 00:39:54,800
but I'm more curious
why you made a logo for the band.

512
00:39:55,640 --> 00:39:59,040
Well, didn't you tell me
to do what I like?

513
00:39:59,960 --> 00:40:02,000
I thought it'd be something about gaming.

514
00:40:03,160 --> 00:40:04,200
I'd better get going.

515
00:40:17,400 --> 00:40:19,080
COMPETITION DAY

516
