686
00:55:57,920 --> 00:55:58,880
Bye.

687
00:56:04,040 --> 00:56:07,280
- Open your present!
- I want to take a picture!

688
00:56:11,320 --> 00:56:12,880
- Open it!
- Open it!

689
00:56:29,400 --> 00:56:31,720
You've been getting home late
every day lately.

690
00:56:31,800 --> 00:56:33,080
Why aren't you heading home?

691
00:56:35,280 --> 00:56:38,800
I feel like I'm getting worse.
The more I do it, the worse I get.

692
00:56:38,880 --> 00:56:40,880
Maybe it's because it's not your passion.

693
00:56:46,640 --> 00:56:48,880
Have you ever noticed
the eyes of someone with a passion?

694
00:56:49,720 --> 00:56:51,000
They have strength.

695
00:56:51,080 --> 00:56:54,520
There's a spark in their eyes that's…
I can't really explain it.

696
00:56:54,600 --> 00:56:57,000
So… I don't have that?

697
00:56:57,080 --> 00:57:00,520
No. You don't have that spark
when you draw.

698
00:57:00,600 --> 00:57:02,280
But I've seen it in you before.

699
00:57:06,200 --> 00:57:07,240
Here.

700
00:57:08,320 --> 00:57:10,280
You're completely different there
than you are now.

701
00:57:13,000 --> 00:57:14,400
When did you see this?

702
00:57:14,480 --> 00:57:15,880
A while ago.

703
00:57:15,960 --> 00:57:17,560
It popped up in my feed.

704
00:57:17,640 --> 00:57:19,520
I guess I've been watching
a lot of game streams.

705
00:57:21,640 --> 00:57:23,480
Did you study architecture
for your family?

706
00:57:28,600 --> 00:57:31,680
Here's my advice.
Why don't you talk to them first?

707
00:57:32,480 --> 00:57:36,320
Trust me. I've been through it.
And this is how it turned out.

708
00:57:37,320 --> 00:57:39,280
I studied something I didn't like.

709
00:57:39,960 --> 00:57:43,200
When I finally started working,
I was miserable.

710
00:57:44,200 --> 00:57:46,240
I thought you liked architecture.

711
00:57:46,320 --> 00:57:48,240
That's why you started teaching it.

712
00:57:49,560 --> 00:57:52,920
I don't like architecture.
I just like educating people.

713
00:57:54,600 --> 00:57:58,080
Honestly, I don't really have
anything to teach anyone, except this.

714
00:57:58,880 --> 00:58:03,800
It took me until I was almost 30
to find my own balance, Putter.

715
00:58:04,960 --> 00:58:07,360
Your time belongs to you.

716
00:58:07,920 --> 00:58:10,880
Don't let it slip away. It's too precious.

717
00:58:12,560 --> 00:58:15,000
At the very least,
I hope you'll try talking to them first.

718
00:58:15,080 --> 00:58:17,080
I'm sure you can find a way together.

719
00:58:17,160 --> 00:58:18,640
Thank you so much.

720
00:58:25,360 --> 00:58:26,880
I've already lit the spark for you.

721
00:58:27,560 --> 00:58:29,120
Now you need to keep the fire going.

722
00:58:29,760 --> 00:58:32,480
Don't let it burn out, your passion.

723
00:58:33,080 --> 00:58:35,160
Go on. Head home.

724
00:58:43,600 --> 00:58:45,800
DON'T GIVE UP EVEN WHEN IT'S HARD! - REBEL

725
00:58:58,200 --> 00:58:59,680
Yeah, okay.

726
00:59:09,800 --> 00:59:10,680
Lee!

727
00:59:33,240 --> 00:59:34,360
Hey, where are you going?

728
00:59:34,440 --> 00:59:35,520
I'm going to take a shower.

729
00:59:35,600 --> 00:59:37,440
I don't want to lie on
the couch while I'm all dirty.

730
00:59:37,520 --> 00:59:39,880
Don't worry about it.
See? I'm already lying down. Come here.

731
00:59:39,960 --> 00:59:42,880
- Hey, no way.
- Come on. Get over here.

732
00:59:46,200 --> 00:59:47,120
How is it?

733
00:59:47,200 --> 00:59:49,240
Your mom's couch is so nice.

734
00:59:49,320 --> 00:59:50,560
It really is comfortable.

735
00:59:51,680 --> 00:59:56,240
<i>Your time belongs to you.</i>

736
00:59:56,320 --> 00:59:57,680
<i>Don't let it slip away.</i>

737
00:59:57,760 --> 01:00:00,600
<i>At the very least,</i>
<i>I hope you'll try talking to them first.</i>

738
01:00:00,680 --> 01:00:02,320
<i>I'm sure you can find a way together.</i>

739
01:00:12,400 --> 01:00:15,080
How should I start talking
to my parents about my dream?

740
01:00:17,040 --> 01:00:19,040
<i>Opening up about your dreams</i>

741
01:00:19,120 --> 01:00:22,280
<i>or your goals in life with your parents</i>
<i>may feel awkward or intimidating at first.</i>

742
01:00:22,360 --> 01:00:25,040
<i>But if you prepare yourself</i>
<i>and choose the right moment,</i>

743
01:00:25,120 --> 01:00:26,720
<i>everything will go much more smoothly.</i>

744
01:00:26,800 --> 01:00:29,120
<i>Try these tips and steps.</i>

745
01:00:32,960 --> 01:00:35,160
So how do I start moving on?

746
01:00:36,560 --> 01:00:40,120
Answer me like
you're a relationship expert.

747
01:00:41,800 --> 01:00:43,120
<i>An expired love</i>

748
01:00:43,200 --> 01:00:45,880
<i>is like a pair of shoes</i>
<i>that rubs your feet raw.</i>

749
01:00:45,960 --> 01:00:49,040
<i>No matter how beautiful they are,</i>
<i>or how much they cost,</i>

750
01:00:49,120 --> 01:00:52,440
<i>if you keep wearing them,</i>
<i>the wound will never heal.</i>

751
01:00:52,520 --> 01:00:57,240
<i>Try taking them off</i>
<i>and find a new pair that fits you better.</i>

752
01:00:57,320 --> 01:00:59,840
<i>Is there anything else</i>
<i>you'd like to tell me?</i>

753
01:00:59,920 --> 01:01:02,240
<i>What's weighing on your mind the most?</i>

754
01:01:04,400 --> 01:01:07,640
FIRST DAY OF SCHOOL BREAK

755
01:01:11,440 --> 01:01:13,360
I'm going back home for a while.

756
01:01:14,240 --> 01:01:16,120
My mom's birthday is coming up.

757
01:01:16,800 --> 01:01:19,360
Sure. How long will you be gone?

758
01:01:19,440 --> 01:01:20,360
Maybe…

759
01:01:21,160 --> 01:01:23,880
about… a week or two.

760
01:01:24,480 --> 01:01:27,320
If you want to invite your friends over,
don't worry about me.

761
01:01:28,840 --> 01:01:30,760
Okay. Thanks.

762
01:01:31,560 --> 01:01:32,840
Yeah.

763
01:01:34,320 --> 01:01:36,080
Thanks for the gift.

764
01:01:37,200 --> 01:01:38,840
So, do you like it?

765
01:01:39,840 --> 01:01:43,200
I freaking love it. The design is sick.

766
01:01:44,560 --> 01:01:46,000
I'm giving it back to you.

767
01:01:50,280 --> 01:01:51,560
I'm heading out. See you.

768
01:01:54,600 --> 01:01:55,480
Wait.

769
01:01:56,880 --> 01:01:58,680
Can I ask why you're giving it back?

770
01:02:00,240 --> 01:02:05,320
Just getting your support
was enough to help me chase my dream.

771
01:02:07,720 --> 01:02:09,240
Your support was all I needed.

772
01:02:14,400 --> 01:02:15,960
Besides Indy,

773
01:02:21,680 --> 01:02:23,640
you're my best friend too.

774
01:02:40,760 --> 01:02:42,240
Yeah, I think so too.

775
01:02:42,320 --> 01:02:44,320
The power of friendship is pretty amazing.

776
01:02:44,400 --> 01:02:45,560
See you.

777
01:05:50,160 --> 01:05:51,840
<i>How are you doing in Bangkok?</i>

778
01:05:52,400 --> 01:05:53,480
<i>Getting used to it yet?</i>

779
01:05:55,080 --> 01:05:56,960
I'm going back to Chiang Mai.

780
01:05:59,520 --> 01:06:00,960
Please tell my mom and dad for me.

781
01:07:05,680 --> 01:07:07,200
Dad, Mom.

782
01:07:07,280 --> 01:07:09,360
I don't want to
continue studying architecture.

783
01:07:09,880 --> 01:07:11,440
<i>Let's break up.</i>

784
01:07:11,520 --> 01:07:13,280
<i>You act just like your friend.</i>

785
01:07:14,480 --> 01:07:16,160
New opportunities
are right around the corner.

786
01:07:17,240 --> 01:07:19,000
<i>You don't have to</i>
<i>force yourself if you don't like it.</i>

787
01:07:19,600 --> 01:07:20,800
<i>If we force this, it'll destroy all of us.</i>

788
01:07:23,480 --> 01:07:26,000
<i>Tungtae. Are you with Putter?</i>

789
01:07:26,080 --> 01:07:27,480
What? He isn't coming back?

790
01:07:29,280 --> 01:07:30,520
<i>I honestly can't just be your friend.</i>
